444
00:24:35,224 --> 00:24:40,324
Politicians create treaty momentum, because votes follow money follows lobbying

445
00:24:40,324 --> 00:24:46,644
follows insurance follows actuarial tables, which is the most boring causal

446
00:24:46,644 --> 00:24:49,864
chain in history but also the most reliable.

447
00:24:50,984 --> 00:24:55,624
Defense contractors hedge, because they can't risk being left out of a profitable

448
00:24:55,624 --> 00:24:56,324
shift.

449
00:24:57,084 --> 00:24:57,964
Pharma pivots,

450
00:24:58,564 --> 00:25:02,704
because adapt or die, which is ironic advice to give an industry that's

451
00:25:02,704 --> 00:25:04,174
supposed to prevent dying.

452
00:25:05,144 --> 00:25:09,944
Billionaires pile in last, because FOMO is powerful in humans generally

453
00:25:09,944 --> 00:25:12,804
and devastating in billionaires specifically,

454
00:25:13,444 --> 00:25:17,984
who have built their identities around being first and cannot tolerate being

455
00:25:17,984 --> 00:25:18,724
last.

456
00:25:20,004 --> 00:25:21,724
Why This Can Work:

457
00:25:21,744 --> 00:25:23,964
The Coordination Problem Has a Price Tag.

458
00:25:25,284 --> 00:25:29,784
Public choice theory predicts that concentrated interests beat diffuse interests.

459
00:25:30,764 --> 00:25:31,264
Always.

460
00:25:31,904 --> 00:25:36,744
Ten lobbyists who each make ten million dollars from war will outfight ten

461
00:25:36,744 --> 00:25:40,724
million patients who each lose ten dollars from disease.

462
00:25:41,524 --> 00:25:45,544
This is Olson's observation, and it's correct, and it's the reason your

463
00:25:45,544 --> 00:25:48,704
species builds weapons better than it cures cancer.

464
00:25:49,804 --> 00:25:52,224
The part Olson didn't account for:

465
00:25:52,284 --> 00:25:55,544
the people getting screwed have ninety times more money.

466
00:25:56,304 --> 00:26:01,444
Concentrated interests (defense, fossil fuels) have roughly five trillion

467
00:26:01,444 --> 00:26:06,324
dollars in market cap and spend one hundred million to one billion dollars

468
00:26:06,324 --> 00:26:08,734
annually on political influence.

469
00:26:09,044 --> 00:26:14,084
Diffuse beneficiaries (everyone who'd benefit from cures) have four hundred

470
00:26:14,084 --> 00:26:18,744
and fifty-four trillion dollars in household wealth and spend approximately

471
00:26:18,744 --> 00:26:24,024
zero dollars on political influence, because of coordination failure, which

472
00:26:24,024 --> 00:26:27,984
is the academic term for "everyone wants it but nobody does anything.".

473
00:26:29,084 --> 00:26:32,224
Having more capital doesn't help if you can't deploy it.

474
00:26:32,744 --> 00:26:34,544
That's Olson's whole point and he's right.

475
00:26:35,144 --> 00:26:40,024
A ninety to one capital advantage means nothing when each individual's share

476
00:26:40,024 --> 00:26:42,024
is too small to motivate action.

477
00:26:42,924 --> 00:26:44,964
Coordination costs eat everything.

478
00:26:45,984 --> 00:26:48,804
This is why your species can't have nice things,

479
00:26:49,464 --> 00:26:53,324
stated in the language of economics so that economists will take it seriously.

480
00:26:54,344 --> 00:26:58,904
Incentive Alignment Bonds are a coordination mechanism disguised as a financial

481
00:26:58,904 --> 00:26:59,444
product.

482
00:27:00,204 --> 00:27:03,484
They turn political change into an investment.

483
00:27:03,624 --> 00:27:06,494
Investors don't need to care about curing disease.

484
00:27:06,904 --> 00:27:08,274
They need to care about returns.

485
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:12,564
The returns happen to require curing disease.

486
00:27:13,104 --> 00:27:17,324
Whether this actually works at scale is an open question (nobody's tried

487
00:27:17,324 --> 00:27:19,624
