488
00:27:19,624 --> 00:27:23,964
if you can make "lobby for health" pay better than "lobby for war,"

489
00:27:24,664 --> 00:27:26,164
lobbyists will lobby for health.

490
00:27:27,004 --> 00:27:30,464
This is not a controversial claim about human nature.

491
00:27:30,964 --> 00:27:34,204
This is the least controversial claim about human nature.

492
00:27:34,244 --> 00:27:39,024
It is, in fact, the only claim about human nature that has never been wrong.

493
00:27:40,024 --> 00:27:43,424
Why the cascade can happen (not "must" happen).

494
00:27:43,804 --> 00:27:48,584
Once I.A.B.s concentrate financial benefits on the pro-health side, politicians

495
00:27:48,584 --> 00:27:51,244
face a new calculation where I.A.B.

496
00:27:51,664 --> 00:27:54,224
benefits outweigh concentrated opposition costs.

497
00:27:55,144 --> 00:27:57,744
Each policy success increases I.A.B.

498
00:27:57,964 --> 00:28:00,524
funding, which strengthens the coalition.

499
00:28:00,724 --> 00:28:04,304
Investors lobby for treaty expansion to increase their returns.

500
00:28:04,484 --> 00:28:06,104
The dynamic reverses:

501
00:28:06,484 --> 00:28:10,104
supporting clinical trial funding becomes the concentrated-benefit option.

502
00:28:10,784 --> 00:28:13,024
The diffuse interest becomes concentrated.

503
00:28:13,504 --> 00:28:15,464
The Olsonian problem dissolves.

504
00:28:15,524 --> 00:28:17,084
Not because humans got better.

505
00:28:17,384 --> 00:28:18,634
Because the math changed.

506
00:28:19,324 --> 00:28:20,524
This isn't inevitable.

507
00:28:20,684 --> 00:28:22,344
It requires sufficient I.A.B.

508
00:28:22,544 --> 00:28:27,424
funding to overcome opposition, and "sufficient" is a number nobody can

509
00:28:27,424 --> 00:28:28,444
calculate in advance.

510
00:28:29,044 --> 00:28:30,394
But the capital exists.

511
00:28:30,624 --> 00:28:32,304
It just needs a reason to move.

512
00:28:33,004 --> 00:28:35,804
On Wishonia, we'd call this "providing a reason."

513
00:28:36,404 --> 00:28:40,244
On Earth, you'd call it "the most important financial product in history"

514
00:28:40,524 --> 00:28:43,544
or "a pipe dream," depending on whether you've read the math.

515
00:28:44,444 --> 00:28:46,124
Why This Scales:

516
00:28:46,224 --> 00:28:46,764
The Ratchet Effect.

517
00:28:47,864 --> 00:28:51,644
Each treaty expansion creates more political incentive funding to lobby

518
00:28:51,644 --> 00:28:53,184
for the next expansion.

519
00:28:53,584 --> 00:28:57,644
At one percent, political incentive funding is two point seven two billion

520
00:28:57,644 --> 00:28:58,564
dollars per year.

521
00:28:59,084 --> 00:29:01,464
At ten percent, that scales to ten times.

522
00:29:01,944 --> 00:29:04,804
Politicians who supported the one percent treaty get rewarded.

523
00:29:05,364 --> 00:29:07,704
Those rewards grow if they push for two percent.

524
00:29:08,244 --> 00:29:11,224
It's a ratchet that only moves in one direction:

525
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:14,224
the direction where people stop dying.

526
00:29:14,504 --> 00:29:16,184
You've built ratchets like this before.

527
00:29:16,484 --> 00:29:17,504
Social Security.

528
00:29:17,564 --> 00:29:18,144
Medicare.

529
00:29:18,464 --> 00:29:23,084
Once they exist, dismantling them is politically suicidal because too many

530
00:29:23,084 --> 00:29:24,344
people depend on them.

531
00:29:24,924 --> 00:29:29,224
The difference is you built those by accident, through crisis and desperation,

532
00:29:29,484 --> 00:29:32,324
and spent decades arguing about whether they were good ideas.

533
00:29:32,964 --> 00:29:35,424
This time, try doing it on purpose.

534
00:29:35,984 --> 00:29:39,524
On Wishonia, we've found that building things on purpose works better than

535
00:29:39,524 --> 00:29:43,744
building them by accident, though I realize this is a controversial position

536
00:29:43,744 --> 00:29:46,924
for a species that invented penicillin by leaving a sandwich out.

537
00:29:59,772 --> 00:30:05,312
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

538
00:30:05,312 --> 00:30:09,532
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

539
00:30:09,532 --> 00:30:13,232
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

540
00:30:13,232 --> 00:30:14,272
war and disease instead.

541
00:30:14,892 --> 00:30:19,232
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

542
00:30:19,232 --> 00:30:23,392
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

543
00:30:23,392 --> 00:30:26,952
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

544
00:30:27,512 --> 00:30:29,712
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

545
00:30:30,252 --> 00:30:34,312
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

546
00:30:34,312 --> 00:30:39,932
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

547
00:30:40,352 --> 00:30:43,912
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

548
00:30:43,912 --> 00:30:45,372
versus clinical trials.

549
00:30:45,652 --> 00:30:46,152
And vote!

550
00:30:46,572 --> 00:30:50,832
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

551
00:30:50,832 --> 00:30:55,452
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

552
00:30:55,452 --> 00:30:58,152
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

553
00:30:58,552 --> 00:30:59,112
Love you, bye!
